{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PASS 1 (asserted-capability) finding: The plan asserts `completion.py` provides an existing `sign_verdict()` helper and the AC commits the workflow sign step to call `completion.sign_verdict()`. This capability claim is REFUTED by the code: `src/rebar/llm/completion.py` has no `sign_verdict` (its `__all__` is COMPLETION_REMEDIATION_GUIDANCE, child_closure_findings, deterministic_child_failure, reconcile_verdict, verify_completion), and its module docstring explicitly states the verifier \"never writes, transitions, signs, or closes.\" Completion-verdict signing actually lives in `rebar._commands.transition_close.sign_completion_verdict()` (line 469), which delegates to the signing seam `rebar.signing.sign_manifest(..., kind=\"completion-verifier\")`. Plan should retarget the sign step to the real signing seam rather than a nonexistent completion.py helper."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785711325393460001,"uuid":"b2b9b963-75a2-4ee5-a5c4-a2d27182183f"}